#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:92
#. Diagram label
msgid "Append `retained` with the reason"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Brief the work"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clean: close the open issue carrying the tracking label (the `label` input), if any, saying why the verdict is clean. Runs only on a clean verdict — on unknown the issue is left untouched and the job fails instead, because could-not-check is never rendered as clean."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close the tracking issue"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:25
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create the tracking label (the `label` input) with --force so it exists before either issue path runs — the close path filters on it too, and on a repository that has never had a finding it would not exist yet. Skipped on an unknown verdict."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:76
#. Diagram label
msgid "Drain: land, close or re-target the open PRs"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:24
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ensure the tracking label exists"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Findings: EDIT the one open issue carrying the tracking label (the `label` input) if there is one, otherwise create it, with the report as the body. One issue edited in place, never a new issue or a comment per run, so the tracking issue never becomes a feed."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:35
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open or EDIT the one tracking issue"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:59
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the sign-off as a requirement-signoff attestation"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:85
#. Diagram label
msgid "Report what would move — sizes, and what breaks"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agent reports and waits: what would move, how large, what in the parent breaks, and the rollback. `deletion-requires-confirmation` is not a courtesy to waive: an agent never removes or relocates a durable artefact on its own initiative."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The entry that makes the log worth reading. A removal was considered and refused, or a preview still stands because a signal fired; without an entry that leaves no trace, and the next person asking \"why is this preview still up\" has nothing to consult. A reason is REQUIRED — the tool refuses without one."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "THE RECORD, and not relaxable: a judgement nobody wrote down is indistinguishable from one never made (`adjudication`, A_RecordEntry). Append one `requirement-signoff` record to `test/attestations/requirement-signoff/<set slug>.attestations.json` — who (kind, id, actor), at, scope (the set or one member), the outcome from the requirement-set code list, the stage it moves the set to, the reason, and the permalink to the issue comment where it was decided — and set the set's `stage` to match. Issue #2405 FR-011 / FR-012. GW_SignoffRecorded after this reads the record back, so this step cannot be skipped by completing it: a sign-off that left no attestation loops here again."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "What the work is and why, what is already measured with its provenance, how it will be done, and what would falsify the approach. The bean is already claimed by the Process_BeanOpen call before this step (bean m8gz), so a sibling session sees the work before the brief is written."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Work the PRs `seed:ready` named until the source settles: land or close the heavy movers and the next layer's PRs, bring the layer's open PRs to five or fewer, and finish any move in flight. Fix a red rehearsal or a discovery miss where it is. Nothing is seeded from here; it goes back to the gateway, which re-asks."
msgstr ""
